# Build output
/build/bin/
/dist/
*.exe
*.syso

# ...but NOT the binaries vendored inside third_party/, which are source, not
# build output. `*.exe` above silently excluded
# third_party/wails-v2.13.0/internal/webview2runtime/MicrosoftEdgeWebview2Setup.exe,
# which webview2installer.go go:embed's. The result compiled on the machine that
# vendored Wails, because the file was sitting there untracked, and failed on
# every fresh clone with
#
#	webview2installer.go:9:12: pattern MicrosoftEdgeWebview2Setup.exe: no matching files found
#
# — but ONLY under -tags production/dev, because an untagged `go build ./...`
# uses main_nocgo.go and never reaches Wails at all. So the Windows gate this
# port was being judged by could not see it.
!third_party/**/*.exe

# Go
/vendor/

# Node
node_modules/
/frontend/dist/
/frontend/wailsjs/

# Local
*.local
.env
registry.bin

# Generated by build/pack-portable.ps1 (~20 MB, rebuilt on demand)
/cmd/portable/payload.zip
/build/dist/
/cmd/portable/rsrc_windows_amd64.syso
.DS_Store
